---
description: >
  BACKEND ARCHITECTURE - /back-end repo
  
  Deployment:
  - Production URL: https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com
  - API Base: https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com/api
  
  Database:
  - Type: Supabase PostgreSQL
  - Connection: Session Pooler (IPv4 compatible)
  - RLS: ENABLED on all tables
  - ORM: Prisma
  - ⚠️ CRITICAL: When adding Supabase Realtime websockets to ANY new table, you MUST add Row Level Security (RLS) policies
    * Without RLS policies, realtime subscriptions will fail silently or expose data
    * Always add policies to /back-end/prisma/migrations/enable_rls.sql
    * Required policies: SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE (matching user access patterns)
    * Ensure proper indexes exist on filter columns (e.g., userId) for performance
    * Ensure user turns on real-time enabled on supabase dashboard
    * MAKE SURE to use DB push when syncing the db, never use prisma migrate dev because that will DELETE all tables
  
  Authentication:
  - Method: JWKS (JSON Web Key Set)
  - JWKS Endpoint: https://kzlurqihzaolhzsbkctf.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
  - Key ID: 3f646428-da10-4054-9125-309e72d9b2e4
  - Algorithm: ES256 (Elliptic Curve)
  - No secret keys needed: Backend fetches public keys from JWKS
  
  API Structure:
  - REST API Only: No WebSocket on backend (removed)
  - Real-time: Frontend uses Supabase Realtime directly
  - Port: 3001 (local), configurable for production
  
  Endpoints:
  PUBLIC (No Auth): GET /health (Health check), POST /api/waitlist (Join waitlist)
  AUTHENTICATED (Requires JWT): GET /api/agents (List user's agents), POST /api/agents (Create agent), GET /api/agents/:id (Get agent + messages), POST /api/agents/:id/messages (Send message), DELETE /api/agents/:id (Soft delete agent), POST /api/format-llm-judge-prompt (Format LLM prompt), GET /api/tools (Get available tools)
  
  ⚠️ ZOD SCHEMA CHANGES REQUIRE APPROVAL:
  - CRITICAL: Any changes to Zod schemas in route files MUST be proposed to the user first
  - Wait for explicit user approval before implementing schema changes
  - This includes: Adding/removing fields, Changing field types, Modifying validation rules, Updating required/optional status
  - Reason: Schema changes affect API contracts and may require frontend updates
  - Process: 1. Propose the schema change to user, 2. Wait for user approval, 3. Implement only after approval
  
  Authentication Middleware (src/middleware/auth.ts):
  1. Extracts JWT from Authorization Bearer header
  2. Parses token header to get kid (Key ID)
  3. Fetches public key from JWKS endpoint (cached 10 minutes)
  4. Verifies JWT signature using public key
  5. Validates issuer, audience, expiration
  6. Extracts user ID from sub claim
  7. Attaches req.user with { id, email, phone }
  
  Database Schema:
  - Schema Location: /back-end/prisma/schema.prisma (single source of truth)
  - All database changes MUST be made through Prisma: 1. Edit schema.prisma, 2. Run npm run prisma:migrate:dev -- --name your_change, 3. Never manually edit the database
  
  Tables with RLS: Agent (User's AI agents - users can only see their own), Message (Chat messages - users can only see messages from their agents), AgentAttentionRequest (Attention requests - users can only see their own), Tool (Available tools - public read), AgentTool (Many-to-many junction - users can only see their agent's tools), Verifier (Agent verifiers - users can only see their agent's verifiers)
  
  Public Tables (No RLS): Waitlist (Public signups - accessed via backend API only)
  
  Agent Statuses: STARTING_UP (Agent initializing), ACTIVE (Agent running), PAUSED (Agent paused), COMPLETED (Agent finished), FAILED (Agent error)
  
  Message Roles: SYSTEM (System messages), AGENT (Agent responses), USER (User messages), TOOL (Tool outputs), STATUS (Status updates)
  
  RLS Policies: All users can only access data where userId = auth.uid()::text
  
  Database Migrations:
  ALWAYS use Prisma migrations to update the database schema. Never manually run SQL.
  Step 1: Edit /back-end/prisma/schema.prisma
  Step 2 (Development): cd back-end && npm run prisma:migrate:dev -- --name your_migration_name (Creates migration in prisma/migrations/, applies to database, regenerates Prisma Client)
  Step 3 (Production): cd back-end && npm run prisma:migrate (Applies pending migrations in production - used in render.yaml)
  
  Public Endpoints: Some tables don't need RLS because they're accessed via backend API. Example - Waitlist: No RLS policy needed, Backend API (POST /api/waitlist) is public, Backend validates and sanitizes all inputs
  
  When adding public endpoints: 1. Add model to Prisma schema (without RLS), 2. Create migration: npm run prisma:migrate:dev -- --name add_table_name, 3. Add route in /back-end/src/routes/, 4. Register in server.ts BEFORE authenticated routes, 5. Test endpoint with curl or seed script
  
  Seeding Data: Test endpoints by hitting them (recommended): cd back-end && npm run seed:waitlist (Tests API endpoint, validates business logic, ensures CORS is configured, catches errors early). Alternative - Direct Prisma seeding: cd back-end && npm run prisma:seed (Runs prisma/seed.ts)
  
  Migration Files: Located in /back-end/prisma/migrations/, Never edit existing migrations, Never delete migrations that have been deployed, Migration names: YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description/migration.sql
  
  Prisma Studio (GUI): View/edit database directly: cd back-end && npm run prisma:studio (Opens at http://localhost:5555)
  
  Environment Variables:
  DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.kzlurqihzaolhzsbkctf:PASSWORD@aws-1-us-east-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
  SUPABASE_URL=https://kzlurqihzaolhzsbkctf.supabase.co
  OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
  ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8080,https://hinavi.ai
  PORT=3001
  NODE_ENV=development
  
  URL Handling (CRITICAL): Always normalize base URLs. Problem: Double slashes (//api/models) break URLs. Solution: Always strip trailing slashes from base URLs before concatenating paths.
  
  Testing:
  Backend Authentication Test: cd back-end && ./test-auth.sh
  Manual Test with Token: cd back-end && ./test-auth-manual.sh ACCESS_TOKEN
  
  Cleanup All Agents and Workers: cd back-end && npm run cleanup:all (Kills any local Python workers, finds all non-deleted agents, terminates Temporal workflows, soft-deletes agents). Environment variable: TEST_TASK_QUEUE (defaults to navi-agent-tasks-quicktest). Use when: Starting fresh after testing, cleaning up before deployment, workers are stuck/misbehaving, orphaned agents in database
  
  Key Files:
  - back-end/src/server.ts (Main Express server - REST API only)
  - back-end/src/middleware/auth.ts (JWKS authentication)
  - back-end/prisma/schema.prisma (Database schema)
  - back-end/prisma/migrations/enable_rls.sql (RLS policies)
  - back-end/test-auth.sh (Automated auth test)

apply:
  when: always
---
